      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "The entire tsadi foot is fused to a vertically extended lower mass with two lateral expansions and a waist. The literal tsadi sheva in למִּצְעָר on page177 and the second tsadi qamats in מִצּאֱצָאֵי on page157 both yield broad foot-plus-stem contours. The target does not independently expose the upper stamp as round rather than transverse. Same-page tsadi patah in הַצַּדִּיק and segol in בְּצֶדֶק are shorter, broader fused bases, but excluding those does not distinguish sheva from qamats. Retain the omission.",
