      },
      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "The first lamed has a rounded terminal bulb fused directly to the descending diagonal, with no second independently delimited stamp. The same-unit לִשְׁפֹּט lamed hiriq has a similar bulb, while לְנָכוֹן lamed sheva has a longer fused stem with shallow expansions. Local לַגֵּרִים lamed patah also extends into a connected descending mass. The amount and placement of fused ink does not uniquely classify the target as a hiriq rather than another obscured mark or the letter terminal. Retain the omission; do not infer absence.",
      "physicalLocator": {
        "id": "wis-19-18-word13-lamed-2-vowel",
        "anchorScalarSpan": [
          68,
