      },
      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "The second lamed ends in a broad connected base with two downward lobes and a small lower notch. Same-page מַאֲכָלֵי lamed tsere has a comparable paired base, and page171 לֵב has a literal detached horizontal pair. However, the target upper boundary is swallowed by the letter terminal: the full contour does not establish two round stamps rather than a thickened transverse bar. The fused lamed patah in לַגֵּרִים shows that a lower bar may join the descending letter, and the target shallow notch cannot alone certify tsere. Retain the omission.",
      "physicalLocator": {
