      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "The kaf preserves a separate central dagesh, but the lower bowl merges with a broad solid shelf. It has no independently delimited point or descending tail. The same-page כַּאֲשֶׁר in source17 has a similarly saturated patah base; כִּי hiriq, כְּמוֹ sheva and מַאֲכָלֵי kaf qamats demonstrate varying fused bulbs and tails. The target broad base alone cannot establish a single printed vowel or source absence. Preserve its dagesh and retain the vowel disclosure.",
